 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "One unit: the reciter joins 56→61 (about 106 s). No weapons, horses, war or punishment drawn, and no present-day reading: Al-Muyassar's naming of a people in 56 is not used; 57:5-8 «فشرد بهم» and 60:7-14 «ترهبون به» are not glossed. The restrictions are kept: 57 «في حال المحاربة… لا يكون لهم عهد», 58 «من قرائن أحوالهم… وأخبرهم», 60 «الساعين في هلاككم». 59:1-5 (their assumption) is not glossed. Hands for «وإن جنحوا للسلم فاجنح لها», geometric for «وتوكل على الله». STAGING v4: c1 (56-57) stays ambient: 57 is a fighting verse (in war; never pictured, its punishment wording not glossed). A seal plate draws on for their pledge (56:6) and undraws as it is broken every time (56:10). c2 (58-59): three disbelievers in a town by day (the people of whom betrayal is feared, then those who disbelieve). A seal plate for the treaty between the two sides (58:4; As-Sa'di: a treaty to leave fighting) that undraws at 58:10, after the words for throwing it back to them on equal terms (both tafsirs: tell them openly there is no treaty). The fear of betrayal is a condition and the throwing back is a command to the Prophet, so nobody acts them (camera only). On 58:10-14 (Allah does not love the traitors; As-Sa'di: it also obliges the Muslims to announce the end openly) the camera stays wide, with no close-up on the treaty people, whose betrayal is only feared; a geometric plate on the Name (58:11); on 59 (they will not escape) the camera holds on the disbelievers and an hourglass for the respite (59:6; As-Sa'di: the wisdom in giving them time). Nobody escapes, fights or is hurt. c3 (60) stays ambient: preparing force and horses against the enemy (fighting verse; no weapon, horse or army drawn); a geometric plate for Allah knowing the hidden enemies (60:20), a coins plate for spending in Allah's path (60:23, ending before the Name; Al-Muyassar: wealth and more) and a growth plate for the full repayment (60:29). c4 (61): a town by day, no war imagery: three disbelievers stand fully in frame on the right and, on 61:2 (they incline), walk to the centre beside three believers on the left (both tafsirs: they incline to leaving the war and want peace); a seal plate for the peace (61:3) and a geometric plate on the Name (61:8). Nobody speaks. The command to incline to it and to rely on Allah is addressed to the Prophet, so the believers make no gesture (camera only); after the walk the camera only goes wide, so no pan drifts to the emptied right side. Cover moved to the peace scene with the seal plate (61:6)."
 },
